@startuml dual-metering
!include _theme.puml
title Indevolt dual metering
left to right direction

component "Atmoce PV\nMC100 · 9 kWp" as pv <<pv>>
component "Simulated Shelly 3EM\nSolar / PV source" as shelly <<solar>>
component "Home load" as load <<load>>
component "Solarman SMD1\nGrid smart meter" as smd1 <<meter>>
component "Utility grid" as grid <<grid>>
component "Home Energy Hub\nSF3000 + SFA3600\nBattery source" as hub <<hub>>

pv -right-> load : <color:#fbbf24>AC</color>
pv .down.> shelly : <color:#4ade80>pv_power via HA</color>
shelly .up.> hub : <color:#4ade80>solar data</color>
load -right-> smd1
smd1 -right-> grid : <color:#fbbf24>net</color>
grid -left-> smd1
smd1 .up.> hub : <color:#a78bfa>grid data</color>

note bottom
  Without a PV meter, the grid meter only sees net import/export —
  not total solar generation.
  Based on Indevolt dual metering docs.
end note

@enduml
